@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Build-local mapped-string canonicalization

start
:Receive a Mode-A parse tree or caller-owned Mode-B tree;<<#DBE4FF>>
:Push the root onto the explicit heap work stack;<<#E5DBFF>>

while (another syntax frame?) is (yes)
  :Map one included tree-sitter node to CpgNodeKind;<<#FFE8CC>>
  :Visit its flat Arc<str> fields and nested TypeInfo vectors;<<#FFF3BF>>
  if (equal content already in the build-local FxHashSet?) then (yes)
    :Clone the canonical Arc handle\nand release the duplicate allocation;<<#D3F9D8>>
  else (no)
    :Retain one Arc handle as this value's canonical owner;<<#C3FAE8>>
  endif
  :Append the node and ordered AST edge to the CPG;<<#DBE4FF>>
  :Push children in reverse source order;<<#E5DBFF>>
endwhile (no)

:Drop the temporary pool;\nthe CPG remains the sole long-lived owner;<<#FFE3E3>>
:Run configured CFG, resolution, and DFG phases;\nreturn the unchanged public CPG shape;<<#B2F2BB>>
stop

legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#DBE4FF>| caller tree and persistent CPG |
  |<#E5DBFF>| explicit heap traversal state |
  |<#FFE8CC>| language mapping boundary |
  |<#FFF3BF>| fixed-depth string visitor |
  |<#D3F9D8>| duplicate ownership collapse |
  |<#C3FAE8>| first-value canonical ownership |
  |<#FFE3E3>| temporary pool lifetime boundary |
  |<#B2F2BB>| unchanged public result |
endlegend
@enduml
